# PM Learnings

These learnings demonstrate how to translate high-level AI product philosophy into practical behaviors for interviewing and day-to-day product execution.

## Theme 1: The AI PM Artifact Shift (Evals & Prototyping)

Traditional PM artifacts—static PRDs, wireframes, and linear roadmaps—are fundamentally misaligned with non-deterministic foundation models.

### Key insights from the conversation
- Evals as the New PRD: You cannot hardcode expected inputs and outputs. Defining what “good” looks like requires building robust evaluation frameworks with clear rubrics for wins and losses.
- The 60-20-20 Sweet Spot: Building features that work 100% with today’s model means you have aimed too low; building features that completely fail is science fiction. The sweet spot is to prototype with enough ambition to learn, while staying grounded in model reality.
- Building as a Default Habit: The best AI PMs are hands-on builders who constantly spin up demos, test competing models, maintain personal prompt libraries, and understand the model’s “vibes and personality.”

### Practical learnings & actionable takeaways
- Start Small with “Mini-Evals”: Don’t wait for complex automated evaluation pipelines. Begin with about 20 curated prompts to build alignment, establish rubrics, and isolate failure modes quickly.
- Prototype at the Edge: When designing new capabilities, intentionally include edge cases that current models struggle with. When the next model tier drops, your product will unlock those gaps almost immediately.
- Build a Personal “Vibe Benchmark”: Maintain a consistent set of 5–10 multi-step prompts—ranging from simple creative tasks to complex agentic workflows—to run across every new model release.

